ss=\"dnd-text\">They were both surprised how little is known about some aspects of this.</span></div></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":4}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/cambridge-ielts-17-academic-listening-1-audio-3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-c17-t1-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/13442-cambridge-ielts-17-academic-listening-1-audio-4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-c17-t1-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p><em>Complete the notes below.</em></p><p><em>Write&nbsp;<strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong>&nbsp;for each answer.</em></p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong><strong>Labyrinths</strong></strong></p><p><strong>Definition</strong></p><ul><li>a winding spiral path leading to a central area</li></ul><p><strong>Labyrinths compared with mazes</strong></p><ul><li>Mazes are a type of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t1-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li></ul><p>–&nbsp; <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t1-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;is needed to navigate through a maze</p><p>–&nbsp; the word ‘maze’ is derived from a word meaning a feeling of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t1-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><ul><li>Labyrinths represent a journey through life</li></ul><p>–&nbsp; they have frequently been used in <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t1-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;and prayer</p><p><strong>Early examples of the labyrinth spiral</strong></p><ul><li>Ancient carvings on <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t1-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;have been found across many cultures</li><li>The Pima, a Native American tribe, wove the symbol on baskets</li><li>Ancient Greeks used the symbol on <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t1-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li></ul><p><strong>Walking labyrinths</strong></p><ul><li>The largest surviving example of a turf labyrinth once had a big <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t1-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;at its centre</li></ul><p><strong>Labyrinths nowadays</strong></p><ul><li>Believed to have a beneficial impact on mental and physical health, e.g., walking a maze can reduce a person’s <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t1-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;rate</li><li>Used in medical and health and fitness settings and also prisons</li><li>Popular with patients, visitors and staff in hospitals</li></ul><p>–&nbsp; patients who can’t walk can use ‘finger labyrinths’ made from <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t1-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><p>–&nbsp; research has shown that Alzheimer’s sufferers experience less <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t1-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/cambridge-ielts-17-academic-listening-1-audio-4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-c17-t1-l-q1","part_id":"en-c17-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-c17-t1-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"table_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"litter","correct_answer_variants":["litter"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_13426_1","order_index":1,"points":1},{"id":"en-c17-t1-l-q2","part_id":"en-c17-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-c17-t1-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"table_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"dogs","correct_answer_variants":["dogs"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[2],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_13426_2","order_index":2,"points":1},{"id":"en-c17-t1-l-q3","part_id":"en-c17-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-c17-t1-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"table_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"insects","correct_answer_variants":["insects"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[3],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_13426_3","order_index":3,"points":1},{"id":"en-c17-t1-l-q4","part_id":"en-c17-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-c17-t1-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"table_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"butterflies","correct_answer_variants":["butterflies"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[4],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_1